{
  "id": "continuity-hypothesis",
  "term": "continuity hypothesis",
  "definition": "The continuity hypothesis is the idea that thinking in dreams and thinking while awake are linked, so dream content reflects aspects of waking-life experience. Research described in the packet supports this connection especially for emotionally important experiences, while also noting that dreams can reorganize and fragment memories in normal ways.",
